   "text": {
    "L1": "Arunima Sinha was a volleyball player before a train attack changed her life.",
    "L2": "In 2011, robbers pushed her off a moving train, and she lost a leg.",
    "L3": "In hospital, she chose a huge goal: to climb Mount Everest.",
    "L4": "A disability did not stop her. With an artificial leg and hard training, she reached the top in 2013.",
    "L5": "Her events show courage and determination: she kept trying instead of giving up.",
    "L6": "Her story shows that training and will can make the impossible possible.",
    "L7": "Use irregular past verbs correctly: become became, begin began, and fight fought.",
    "L8": "Now put Arunima's main events in the order they happened."
   },
